North Korea won't unilaterally dismantly dismantling unconfidence
North Korea's foreign secretary told the U.N. on Saturday that the ongoing sanctions had overwhelmed dissolution against the United States and that the country in no way would unilaterally relinquish its nuclear weapons in such circumstances.
Ri Yong Ho told an annual general meeting of the global institution that North Korea had taken "substantial accommodating steps" over the past year, such as halting nuclear and missile tests, dismantling a nuclear testing site and a commitment not to spread nuclear weapons and nuclear technologies.
"But we don't see any corresponding reaction from the U.S.," he added.
