HIV/Aids:Chain reports 14% increase in new cases
"China has announced a 14% increase in the number of its citizens living with HIV and AIDS.
Health officials say more than 82,000 people are infected in the country.
More than 40,000 new cases have been announced for the second quarter of 2018 alone.
The vast majority of new cases were transmitted sexually, a change compared to the past.
Traditionally, HIV spread rapidly in some parts of China as a result of infected blood transfusions.
However, the number of people who became infected with HIV in this way was reduced to almost zero, Chinese health officials said at a conference in Yunnan province.
Year-on-a year-on-year, the number of people living with HIV and Aids in China has risen by 100,000 people.
Sexual HIV transmission is an acute problem in China's LGBT community.
Homosexuality was decriminalized in China in 1997, but discrimination against LGBT people is still widespread.
As a result of the country's conservative values, the study estimates that 70-90% of men who have had sexual intercourse with a man will eventually get married to a woman.
A number of cases of transmission of the disease result from the lack of sexual protection in these relationships.
Since 2003, the Chinese government has voilished a general approach to medicines for HIV as part of efforts to address this problem.
